/target/
/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/dist/
/vendor/external/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# maturin editable builds drop the compiled extension next to its type stub. maturin names
# it per platform — _engine.abi3.so (Linux), _engine.pyd (Windows), _engine.abi3.dylib
# (macOS) — so the rule is EXTENSION-scoped, not filename-scoped: the original single-name
# rule was written on Linux and left the Windows artifact untracked-and-unignored, which is
# how it turned up as a staging candidate the first time this repo was built on Windows.
# `_engine.pyi` is the TRACKED type stub and is deliberately not matched by any line below.
/crates/mantis-bridge/python/mantis/_engine*.so
/crates/mantis-bridge/python/mantis/_engine*.pyd
/crates/mantis-bridge/python/mantis/_engine*.dylib
# artifact dirs are never tracked (CI gate 6 is the enforcement; this is defense in depth)
/reports/
/checkpoints/
/logs/
/benchmarks/
# scratch/audit workspace — never tracked
/tmp/
